  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Guests, firms and travellers pay for reliable service and smooth planning. They judge you by field evidence and how you handle problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is staying calm and polite while fixing the actual problem.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA in hospitality, tourism and aviation management: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools handle bookings, draft itineraries and answer routine questions. Routine desk work shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Human warmth, judgment in a crisis and local knowledge hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for planning drafts; later, own service quality and partnerships.
  </p>

